-- erwartet: C001
-- Lane 142, CForm doubleTyp, mixed arm. One `float` side makes the node a float
-- computation for the checker, but C widens the `double` side and computes in
-- double: 7400 of 200000 sampled cases differ from the float computation, the
-- same silent-widening class the `f` suffix guards against (39 990 of 200 000
-- on literals). There is no conversion form (the F005 shape for integers), so
-- the emitter refuses mixed `float`/`double` arithmetic by name. Pure-double
-- and pure-float nodes are unaffected (both sides read the same width), and so
-- are comparisons (widening preserves the value) and literals (typeless until
-- the neighbour decides). The corpus holds no mixed node (scan over 662 units);
-- this unit proves the refused path. Checker half merge-verified.
module probe::misch142 {
impl fn mische(a : f64, b : f32) -> f64
    effects { pure }
    costs   <= 8 ops
{
    return a + b;
}
}
